@@ -0,0 +1,246 @@
+id: 2026-10-13-test-gate-follow-ups
+title: Test and typecheck gate follow-ups, and a unit-test run that never starts the e2e suite
+priority: normal
+area: infra
+type: correctness
+delivery: code-patch
+intent: >
+  Follow up the 2026-10-10 and 2026-10-12 test and typecheck gate notes with the gaps that adopting
+  them exposed.
+
+  Typecheck cache. Every typecheck target (the one tools/nx-plugins/typecheck.js gives each project,
+  and the ones written in apps/api/project.json and apps/web/project.json) lists
+  `{workspaceRoot}/pnpm-lock.yaml` among its inputs. The plugin exports typecheckTarget, and the
+  runner spec checks all three carry the lockfile.
+
+  Declaration files. scripts/typecheck-project.mjs no longer skips every .d.ts when it looks for
+  uncovered files. A tracked, hand-written declaration file (a global augmentation, a `declare
+  module` shim) that no checked config includes is reported like any other uncovered source.
+  Declarations under build output and typegen folders (dist, build, out, out-tsc, coverage,
+  node_modules, .react-router, +types) are still skipped as generated. apps/web/app-load-context.d.ts
+  surfaced this way; apps/web/tsconfig.app.json and tsconfig.spec.json now include it.
+
+  Workspace root typecheck. scripts/ and tools/ each get a tsconfig.json (strict, Node types,
+  bundler resolution, `**/*.ts`), checked by the same runner through a new root script
+  `pnpm typecheck:workspace` (`node scripts/typecheck-project.mjs scripts && node
+  scripts/typecheck-project.mjs tools`). `pnpm typecheck` runs it after `nx run-many -t typecheck`,
+  and CI runs it as its own step. Neither folder becomes an Nx project, so no lint, test or build
+  target appears for them. tools/fragment-to-select.ts imported a module that no longer exists in
+  the repo (../scripts/doctor-sdk-contract-analysis); that analysis ships in @nestledjs/doctor, which
+  exports buildPrismaSelectFromFragments and its types, so the tool imports it from there.
+
+  Windows spawn options. ownedProcessOptions() in apps/api-e2e/src/support/api-process.ts takes
+  `{ shell }`, default true. With no argument it behaves as before (detached on POSIX, a shell on
+  Windows for pnpm's .cmd shim). `ownedProcessOptions({ shell: false })` is for spawning an
+  executable directly, such as process.execPath. Through cmd.exe, an unquoted path containing a
+  space is split there and the spawn fails. The native spec runs every cleanup case for both
+  launches, pnpm-style through a shell and node directly.
+
+  Unit-test runs no longer start the e2e suite. The api-e2e `test` target was the e2e wrapper, so
+  `nx run-many -t test` (and `pnpm test`, and CI's `pnpm test:coverage`) started the real API e2e
+  and, when the database was unreachable, the Docker Compose test database. `api-e2e:e2e` is now the
+  only target that runs the suite. `api-e2e:test` is an `nx:noop` that depends on
+  `api-e2e:test-support`, the database-free support suite. scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh calls
+  `api-e2e:e2e`. CI runs unit tests (`pnpm test:coverage`) and then the e2e suite as its own step,
+  `pnpm exec nx run api-e2e:e2e -- --coverage`, with TEST_DATABASE_URL on that step only.
+
+  Dead Jest files. Remove apps/api-e2e/jest.config.ts and jest.config.simple.ts (the suite runs on
+  Vitest), drop them from apps/api-e2e/tsconfig.spec.json, and replace its `"types": ["jest",
+  "node"]` with `["node"]`. The specs import describe/it/expect from vitest.
+
+  run-tests.sh. When the caller supplied TEST_DATABASE_URL and that database is unreachable, the
+  wrapper fails with a message instead of starting the repo's Docker Compose test database, which
+  would not be at that URL and would replace a stopped container the developer owns. It starts its
+  own test database only when no URL was supplied. scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh (`pnpm test:e2e`)
+  likewise neither starts nor stops the repo's test container when TEST_DATABASE_URL is supplied,
+  and forwards every argument to `api-e2e:e2e` (it used to forward only the first, dropping e.g.
+  `--coverage` after a file filter). The
+  wrapper runs under `set -euo pipefail`. The Vitest run is bracketed by `set +e`
+  / `set -e` so its status is still captured from PIPESTATUS. The summary match uses a here-string
+  rather than `echo | grep -q`, because under pipefail the writer's SIGPIPE would turn a found
+  failure into "no match". The passed-count pipeline ends in `|| true` so no match is a count of
+  zero. Cleanup no longer swallows a failure to stop a test database the wrapper started: it prints
+  a warning on stderr and leaves the result unchanged. scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh does the same, and
+  its comment no longer describes the removed exit-code adjustment.
+
+  Coverage. libs/web's Vitest coverage excludes src/__mocks__/** and src/test-setup.ts.
+
+  Generated route types in specs. apps/web/tsconfig.spec.json includes `.react-router/types/**/*`
+  and sets `rootDirs: [".", "./.react-router/types"]`, as tsconfig.app.json does, so a spec that
+  imports a route using `./+types/...` typechecks.
+
+  Typed e2e GraphQL helpers. TestHelpers.graphql and authenticatedGraphql in
+  apps/api-e2e/src/support/test-helpers.ts are `<TData = unknown>` and return
+  `AxiosResponse<GraphQLResponse<TData>>`, with GraphQLResponse, GraphQLErrorResponse and
+  GraphQLVariables exported. Callers pass the type of the selection they read, so `.data.data` is
+  no longer `any`. The helpers' own register/login/verify/reset/me calls are typed the same way, as
+  is the local gql helper in organization-billing.spec.ts. The specs pass their response types.
+
+  Disposable test database. Global setup refuses, before it connects, a TEST_DATABASE_URL that is
+  not disposable: the host must be localhost, 127.0.0.1 or ::1, and the database name must end in
+  `_test`. `E2E_ALLOW_NON_DISPOSABLE_DB=1` lets a run through anyway, with a warning. The
+  from-scratch reset (taken when migrate deploy reports P3005) requires a disposable database
+  regardless of the opt-out, and now uses the same rule, so a name like `test_data` is no longer
+  reset. The checks live in the new, side-effect-free
+  apps/api-e2e/src/support/database-guards.ts with its own spec in the support suite. Setup logs
+  the database by host and name rather than its full URL.
+
+  Database probe. Global setup's readiness probe is the pg runner by default and needs no psql.
+  `E2E_DATABASE_PROBE=psql` runs `psql -At -c 'SELECT 1'` from PATH instead, with the URL passed
+  as PGHOST/PGPORT/PGUSER/PGPASSWORD/PGDATABASE (and PGSSLMODE) so the password never reaches a
+  command line. This is for a repo whose lifecycle tests stand in for the database with a stub
+  psql.
+
+  SQL splitter. apps/api-e2e/src/support/sql-runner.mjs keeps a backslash-escaped quote inside an
+  escape string (E'it\'s'), and no longer opens a dollar quote at a `$` inside an identifier
+  (price$usd$), including after a non-ASCII identifier character (café$usd$), which `\w` does not
+  match. Nested block comments are still not tracked; its doc comment says so.
+why: >
+  Each of these left a gate reporting green, or a run doing more than it said. A dependency upgrade
+  that changed types replayed a cached typecheck, because the inputs named only typescript. An
+  uncovered hand-written .d.ts passed silently, since the runner skipped all declarations. The root
+  scripts and tools were never typechecked at all, which is how a broken import in
+  tools/fragment-to-select.ts went unnoticed. `nx run-many -t test`, the normal unit-test command,
+  started the API e2e suite and a Docker database, so a unit-test run on a laptop or a CI job
+  without Docker could hang or fail for reasons that had nothing to do with unit tests.
+
+  Global setup migrated, pushed and seeded whatever TEST_DATABASE_URL named. A URL copied from
+  DATABASE_URL would have had its schema rewritten. Spawning node directly with the Windows shell
+  option failed for any Node install path containing a space. Under the wrapper's old `set +e`, an
+  unexpected command failure went unnoticed, and a test database the wrapper could not stop was
+  never mentioned. Specs that import routes could not typecheck once routes used generated types.
+  The e2e GraphQL helpers returned `any`, so a spec could read a field the query never selected and
+  still compile.
+affectedPaths:
