+  - apps/api-e2e/src/support/api-process.native.spec.ts
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/support/database-guards.ts
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/support/database-guards.spec.ts
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/support/global-setup.ts
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/support/e2e-runner.spec.ts
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/support/sql-runner.mjs
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/support/sql-runner.spec.ts
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/support/test-helpers.ts
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/**/*.spec.ts
+  - scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh
+verification:
+  - node --test scripts/typecheck-project.spec.mjs
+  - pnpm exec nx run-many -t typecheck --parallel=1 --skip-nx-cache
+  - pnpm typecheck:workspace
+  - pnpm exec nx run-many -t lint --parallel=1
+  - pnpm exec nx run-many -t test --parallel=1
+  - pnpm exec nx run api-e2e:test-support --skip-nx-cache
+  - pnpm exec nx run api-e2e:e2e
+  - pnpm run nestled-doctor
+agentHints:
+  - >
+    Migrating the api-e2e targets: if project.json has a `test` target that runs the e2e wrapper (or
+    the Vitest executor against the e2e config), make `e2e` the only target that runs the suite and
+    turn `test` into `{"executor": "nx:noop", "dependsOn": ["test-support"]}`. Then change every
+    caller of `api-e2e:test` that means the e2e suite (scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh, package.json
+    scripts, CI, docs) to `api-e2e:e2e`. If CI got its e2e run from `pnpm test`/`pnpm test:coverage`,
+    add an explicit `nx run api-e2e:e2e -- --coverage` step with TEST_DATABASE_URL and the service
+    containers, or the e2e suite silently stops running in CI. Never run `run-many -t test` in a
+    way that starts e2e. Check with `nx run-many -t test` that no `api-e2e:e2e` runs and no
+    container starts.
+  - >
+    Disposable-database guard: global setup now refuses a TEST_DATABASE_URL that is not on
+    localhost/127.0.0.1/::1 or whose name does not end in `_test`. If CI reaches its database by a
+    service hostname (container jobs) or the test database has another name, rename it to *_test
+    where you can; otherwise set E2E_ALLOW_NON_DISPOSABLE_DB=1 on that job only. Lifecycle or
+    support tests that run global setup with fixture URLs must use a local *_test URL or set the
+    opt-out in their env. The from-scratch reset is stricter than before (it needs `_test` at the
+    end of the name), so a database named like `test_app` must be renamed or recreated by hand.
+  - >
+    If the project's lifecycle tests stand in for the database with a stub psql on PATH, set
+    E2E_DATABASE_PROBE=psql in those tests rather than restoring a psql-only probe. Otherwise keep
+    the pg-runner default. The wrapper's own probe (run-tests.sh) always uses the pg runner.
+  - >
+    Custom lib typecheck targets: a project.json `typecheck` that is a plain `tsc -p tsconfig.lib.json
+    && tsc -p tsconfig.spec.json` with no dependsOn should be deleted, and the plugin's target
+    replaces it. A target that has dependsOn (for example a prisma generate) or needs an explicit
+    config list becomes `node scripts/typecheck-project.mjs <projectRoot> [configs...]`, keeps its
+    dependsOn, and adds `{workspaceRoot}/pnpm-lock.yaml` and
+    `{workspaceRoot}/scripts/typecheck-project.mjs` to its inputs.
+  - >
+    `api:build` in dependsOn: if the project's global setup starts the built API from dist rather
+    than `nx serve api`, keep `api:build` in the e2e target's dependsOn (alongside test-support).
+    Without it, the e2e run tests a stale build.
+  - >
+    Duplicate Vite: to check for a second Vite after removing app-level @react-router/dev or
+    @types/node, look in pnpm-lock.yaml (for example `grep -E "^  vite@" pnpm-lock.yaml`), not in
+    node_modules/.pnpm. That folder keeps stale entries until it is pruned, so it can show two
+    versions after the lock has one.
+  - >
+    The PASSED rule is runner-neutral: an e2e run passes only when tests ran, none failed and at
+    least one passed. It is never a cached result and never passWithNoTests. A repo whose e2e
+    runs on Jest implements it from Jest's JSON output (`--json --outputFile`): numFailedTests == 0,
+    numFailedTestSuites == 0, numPassedTests > 0, and a zero exit, with Jest's passWithNoTests off
+    and the target uncached.
+  - >
+    @types/pg: if the lockfile already resolves @types/pg transitively, add that exact version to
+    devDependencies. Never downgrade it, and avoid a caret range that would bump it on the next
+    install.
+  - >
+    Common typecheck fixes seen when adopting the runner. A lib that compiles another lib's .tsx
+    through path mapping needs `jsx` set (TS6142). Spec configs need `target: es2022` (or later)
+    for top-level await. TS2308 `export *` name collisions need explicit re-exports of the
+    conflicting names. Storybook stories typed from the meta (`StoryObj<typeof meta>`) break on
+    union props, so type them from the component (`StoryObj<typeof Component>`).
+  - >
+    SonarCloud: where sonar.sources includes scripts/, add `node --test
+    --experimental-test-coverage --test-reporter=lcov --test-reporter-destination=<file>
+    scripts/typecheck-project.spec.mjs` (or equivalent) to CI's coverage collection, list that lcov
+    in sonar.javascript.lcov.reportPaths, and treat `**/*.spec.mjs` as tests (sonar.tests /
+    sonar.test.inclusions). Otherwise the runner counts as uncovered new code and the new-code
+    coverage gate fails.
+  - >
+    A repo already at 0 uncovered files after the earlier notes should expect no new typecheck
+    errors from the runner change itself. The only new reports are hand-written .d.ts files that no
+    config includes (add each to the config whose code it types, as apps/web did with
+    app-load-context.d.ts), plus whatever scripts/ and tools/ contain once typecheck:workspace
+    checks them.
+  - >
+    scripts/ and tools/ typecheck: copy the two tsconfig.json files and the `typecheck:workspace`
+    script (package.json is not mirrored by template promotion, so add the script and the
+    `pnpm typecheck` chaining by hand). If a script imports generated code (the Prisma client), run
+    it after the Nx typecheck, which generates first. A script that is dead or broken may be
+    deleted instead of fixed. If tools/fragment-to-select.ts still imports
+    ../scripts/doctor-sdk-contract-analysis, import from '@nestledjs/doctor' instead.
+  - >
+    Typed GraphQL helpers: after the default becomes `unknown`, every spec reading `.data.data`
+    from TestHelpers.graphql/authenticatedGraphql fails typecheck until it passes a type matching
+    its selection set. Add small local types per spec. Do not pass `any`. Calls that only read
+    `errors` need no type argument.
+  - >
+    Code that spawns process.execPath (or another executable that is not a .cmd shim) with
+    ownedProcessOptions() should pass `{ shell: false }`. Leave pnpm/npx spawns on the default.
+  - >
+    If the project's run-tests.sh differs from the template's, adopt `set -euo pipefail` with care.
+    Wrap the test run in `set +e`/`set -e`, use here-strings for `grep -q` on captured output, and
+    add `|| true` to count pipelines that may match nothing. Run the wrapper spec (e2e-runner.spec.ts)
+    and confirm a broken test and a zero-test run still fail.
